<h2 class="doc-h2">Actions</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The trigger needs a name that says which row. "Actions" fifteen times is fifteen buttons a
    screen reader cannot tell apart.
</p>
<Example Source="TableActions.razor"><TableActions /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Data Table</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    shadcn's is TanStack Table wired to this. On static SSR there is no client-side table state to
    manage: the toolbar is a GET form, the URL is the state, and the server answers — so the view
    is bookmarkable and the back button works. The full version is on the
    <a href="/blocks">Blocks</a> page.
</p>
